  "plain": "A podcast host, Jesse Michels, notes that the current head of AARO, the Pentagon office set up to investigate unidentified objects, is a former NSA man, the NSA being the US agency that intercepts communications. Michels uses this to float an idea: that releasing information about UFOs bit by bit may be a way to get the public to gather intelligence for the government, which would mean the slow disclosure is a deliberate tactic."
